## Ignore Visual Studio temporary files, build results, and
## files generated by popular Visual Studio add-ons.
##
## See https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/master/VisualStudio.gitignore

# User-specific files
*.rsuser
*.suo
*.user
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

# User-specific files (MonoDevelop/Xamarin Studio)
*.userprefs

# Build results
[Dd]ebug/
[Dd]ebugPublic/
[Rr]elease/
[Rr]eleases/
x64/
x86/
[Aa][Rr][Mm]/
[Aa][Rr][Mm]64/
bld/
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Ll]og/

# Visual Studio 2015/2017 cache/options directory
.vs/
# Uncomment if you have tasks that create the TestResults folder
#TestResults/

# MSTest test Results
[Tt]est[Rr]esults/
[Bb]uild[Ll]og.*

# NUnit
*.VisualState.xml
TestResult.xml

# Build log of MSBuild
*.apexlog
*.log

# Diagnostic Device Log
*.diaglog

# NuGet Packages
*.nupkg
# The packages folder can be ignored because of Package Restore
**/[Pp]ackages/*
# except build/, which is used as an MSBuild target.
!**/[Pp]ackages/build/
# Uncomment if using NuGet repositories to store project specific packages (not recommended)
# !**/[Pp]ackages/

# Microsoft Azure Build Output
csx/
*.build.csdef

# Microsoft Azure Cloud Service Projects
*.celog

# Every Microsoft Office temporary file
~$*

# Others
*.Cache
ClientBin/
~$*
*~
*.dbmdl
*.dbproj.schemaview
*.jfm
*.pfx
*.publishsettings
orleans.codegen.cs

# Including web configuration files
# web.config
# web.Debug.config
# web.Release.config

# Since there are multiple workflows, you may decide to ignore these files
# based on your personal preference.
# libman.json
# .essentials
# .stylecop
# .DS_Store
# .gitattributes
# .gitignore
# .editorconfig
# .browserslistrc
# .node-version
# .npmrc
# .nvmrc
# .yarnrc
# .yarnrc.yml
# package-lock.json
# # Reports
Reports/
TestResults/
[Rr]eports/
*.svg
build_output.txt
tests/**/Reports/
.vs
/*.user
!LICENSE.txt

